{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":274243,"duration_api_ms":274381,"ttft_ms":6021,"ttft_stream_ms":5088,"time_to_request_ms":24,"num_turns":15,"result":"# KovaForge Skills Repository — Review & Improvement Plan\n\n**TLDR:** The repo (58 skills) has a genuinely good governance spec in AGENTS.md, but nothing enforces it, and actual compliance is low: 4 skills have broken YAML frontmatter (likely invisible to discovery), 5 pairs of skills are duplicates (two with *contradictory* instructions), 24 skills have dangling `related_skills` from an unpropagated mass rename, 8 skills are 10-line stubs, and 41 hardcode `/Users/mike` paths. The single highest-leverage fix is a CI lint script — most of the rest is one-time cleanup that the lint then keeps fixed.\n\nI parsed all 58 SKILL.md frontmatters programmatically, checked body sections against AGENTS.md Part 4, validated every `related_skills` link in both directions, diffed suspected duplicates, and pulled per-skill git history. Findings below are from that audit, not sampling.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Current state\n\n**What's healthy:** No secrets found anywhere (Rule 8 ✓). All parseable skills have ≥3 tags. 53–54/58 have version/author/license. The repo is young and active (everything touched May 25 – June 11, 2026), so staleness isn't the problem — **consistency and integrity are**. AGENTS.md itself is a strong spec; the gap is entirely between spec and reality.\n\n**The seven problems, with evidence:**\n\n1. **Broken frontmatter (4 skills).** `brainrepo`, `kovaforge-doccontrol`, `research-output-path`, and `safe-public-posting` have unquoted colons in their `description` (e.g. `Triggers on: \"post this\"`), which makes the YAML unparseable. Any tag-based discovery tooling that parses YAML cannot see these skills at all. `safe-public-posting` is the worst case — it's a *safety guardrail* skill that is simultaneously broken and a 10-line stub.\n\n2. **Duplicate/contradictory skills (5 pairs, ~17% of the repo).**\n   - `delegation-research` vs `research-delegation` — same purpose, **contradictory delegation maps** (one routes research to Milena/Nadia with specific models; the other routes to Nadia/Mikhail/Viktor/Declan). An agent's behavior depends on which one it happens to find.\n   - `bitwarden` vs `bitwarden-secrets` — `bitwarden` v2.0.0 says \"the `bw` CLI is deprecated, use BSM\"; `bitwarden-secrets` says \"use the bitwarden skill for the user vault (bw CLI)\". Contradictory.\n   - `github-model-sync` vs `forge-github-model-sync` — byte-identical descriptions; the *newer* frontmatter (v1.0.1) is in `forge-`, but the actual script lives only in `github-model-sync`. Fragmented, not just duplicated.\n   - `research-local-gemma` vs `local-gemma-sidecar` — full skill vs stub of the same thing; `research-local-gemma`'s own `name:` field is literally `local-gemma-sidecar`. The benchmark reference file exists in both folders **with divergent content**.\n   - `doccontrol` vs `kovaforge-doccontrol` — same DocControl API at dc.delpach.com, authored separately by Aoife and Vladislava.\n\n3. **Relationship graph is badly degraded (Rule 6).** 24 skills have dangling `related_skills` refs; 26 have non-reciprocal links; 6 have none. The dominant cause is systematic: ~14 skills still reference old `vladislava-*` names (e.g. `vladislava-xerahs-kfip-pipeline`) — skills were renamed to drop the prefix but no reference was updated. Others point at skills that never existed here (`llama-cpp`, `antigravity`, `github-auth`, `duckdb-csv-import`).\n\n4. **Body structure compliance is low (Part 4).** Matching headings generously: Overview 9/58, Execution 32/58, Env Vars 24/58, Verification Checklist 29/58, Known Pitfalls 36/58. Eight skills are pure stubs (frontmatter + title, zero body): `qmd`, `playwright-cli`, `safe-public-posting`, `bank-statement-bookkeeping`, `discord-role-sync`, `frontend-skill`, `gbrain-oauth`, `local-gemma-sidecar`. Notably, `playwright-cli` has **9 reference files** and `bank-statement-bookkeeping` has 2 — real content with no body to route agents to it. (Caveat: heading-regex matching can miss renamed sections, so treat the Overview count as \"lacks a recognizable Overview heading,\" not \"has no intro.\")\n\n5. **Two competing frontmatter schemas.** 22 skills use `metadata.hermes.tags` (what AGENTS.md mandates); 36 use top-level `tags:`/`related_skills:`. Any discovery tool reads one shape and misses the other half of the repo.\n\n6. **Portability (Rule 4) is broadly violated.** 41/58 skills hardcode `/Users/mike/...` paths; only 3 declare `required_environment_variables` and 5 declare `required_commands` — despite AGENTS.md Part 5 containing an exact path-patching table for this.\n\n7. **Identity drift + hygiene.** 5 skills where `name:` ≠ folder name (`delegation-claude-code`→`claude-code`, `delegation-codex`→`codex`, `hermes-openclaw-ops`→`hermes-openclaw-ops-maintenance`, `research-dogfood`→`dogfood`, `research-local-gemma`→`local-gemma-sidecar`). Two `.pyc` files are git-tracked in `monitor-crypto-youtube` (added before the `.gitignore` rule). `.hub/` metadata is effectively empty.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Prioritized improvements\n\n### P1 — High impact, low effort (do first)\n\n| # | Improvement | Effort | Impact |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Add `scripts/validate-skills.py` + run it in CI / pre-commit.** Checks: YAML parses, `name`==folder, required frontmatter fields, ≥3 tags, every `related_skills` target exists, required body headings present, no `/Users/mike` outside documented-default tables, no tracked `.pyc`. My audit script is ~80% of this already. | ~half day | Prevents *all* recurrence; turns every other fix into a one-time cost |\n| 2 | **Fix the 4 broken-YAML frontmatters** (quote the descriptions). | 15 min | Restores 4 skills — including the safety-critical `safe-public-posting` — to discoverability |\n| 3 | **Script-fix dangling refs:** strip stale `vladislava-` prefixes, map `claude-code`→`delegation-claude-code`, `codex`→`delegation-codex`, etc.; delete refs to skills that don't exist (`llama-cpp`, `antigravity`, …) or create them deliberately. | 1–2 hrs | Repairs the discovery graph for 24 skills at once |\n| 4 | **Resolve the 5 duplicate pairs.** Merge `github-model-sync`+`forge-github-model-sync` (keep one name, move the script). Delete the `local-gemma-sidecar` stub, fold content into one skill whose `name` matches its folder. Reconcile `delegation-research`/`research-delegation` into one canonical delegation map — this needs a human decision on which map is correct. Same for `doccontrol`/`kovaforge-doccontrol` and the `bitwarden` pair (decide: is `bw` deprecated or not, and say it once). | ~half day + 3 owner decisions | Eliminates contradictory agent behavior; –5 skills of maintenance surface |\n\n### P2 — High impact, medium effort\n\n| # | Improvement | Effort | Impact |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 5 | **Pick ONE frontmatter schema and migrate.** Recommendation: top-level `tags:`/`related_skills:` — it's already the 36-skill majority, it's simpler, and it's what the YAML-broken stubs were converging on anyway. Update AGENTS.md Part 3 to match, and have the linter reject the other shape. | ~half day (scriptable) | Discovery tooling sees 100% of skills instead of ~60% |\n| 6 | **Backfill or deprecate the 8 stubs.** Minimum viable body: Overview with trigger, pointer index into `references/`, verification checklist. `playwright-cli` and `qmd` are quick wins (content already exists in references). Anything not worth backfilling gets `status: deprecated` rather than silent rot. | 1–2 days | Converts dead weight (esp. 9 orphaned playwright reference docs) into usable skills |\n| 7 | **Path-portability pass** using AGENTS.md Part 5's own substitution table, worst offenders first (`codex-cli-weekly-update`:15, `xerahs-url-publishing`:13, `xerahs-hourly-sweep`:13, `gmail-monitor`:11, `finance-investment-report`:11). Backfill `required_environment_variables`/`required_commands` as you touch each. | 2–3 days spread out | Rule 4 compliance; skills become usable on any machine |\n\n### P3 — Lower urgency\n\n8. **Reciprocity pass** on `related_skills` (the linter from #1 can auto-suggest the missing back-link).\n9. **Fix the 5 name/folder mismatches** (pick the folder name as canonical; update any cron jobs per AGENTS.md Part 10 step 12).\n10. **`git rm --cached` the two tracked `.pyc` files.**\n11. **Generate an `INDEX.md` catalog** (name, description, tags, related) from frontmatter as a CI artifact — human-browsable, and a smoke test that every frontmatter parses.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Governance recommendations (anti-degradation)\n\n1. **Enforce, don't document.** AGENTS.md already says everything; the failure mode is unenforced rules. The linter (P1#1) as a required CI check on the GitHub remote is the only recommendation here that changes the trajectory.\n2. **Rename protocol:** a rename isn't done until `grep -r old-name */SKILL.md` is clean. The `vladislava-*` fallout (14 dangling refs) is what happens without this. The linter's dangling-ref check makes it automatic.\n3. **One schema, stated once.** After #5, AGENTS.md Part 3 must show only the surviving shape. Half the drift here looks like authors copying whichever skill they saw last.\n4. **Duplicate gate at creation time:** AGENTS.md §6.1 already says \"check existing skills first\" — add to the PR/commit checklist: \"searched tags + descriptions for overlap; nearest skill is X; this differs because Y.\" The doccontrol pair (two authors, same API, 17 days apart) is the cost of skipping it.\n5. **Deprecation convention:** `status: deprecated` + `superseded_by:` frontmatter fields instead of deleting or abandoning, so `related_skills` chains and cron references degrade gracefully.\n6. **Stub policy:** a SKILL.md with no body fails lint. If the content lives in `references/`, the body must at least index it.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Highest-value individual skills to patch first\n\n1. **`safe-public-posting`** — broken YAML *and* stub, but it's the safety gate for public posting. Highest risk-per-line in the repo.\n2. **`delegation-research` / `research-delegation`** — contradictory routing tables actively steer agents differently. Merge after the owner picks the correct map.\n3. **`bitwarden` / `bitwarden-secrets`** — contradictory credential guidance; secrets handling shouldn't be ambiguous.\n4. **`github-model-sync` / `forge-github-model-sync`** — version-fragmented (new frontmatter in one, the script in the other); whichever an agent picks, it gets half the skill.\n5. **`qmd`** — stub, but referenced by 3 other skills (`brainrepo`, `qmd-daily-update`, `local-gemma-sidecar`), so its emptiness propagates through discovery chains.\n6. **`kovaforge-doccontrol` / `doccontrol`** — duplicate API skill; also `kovaforge-doccontrol` is one of the 4 YAML-broken.\n7. **`playwright-cli`** — cheapest big win: 9 reference docs already written, just needs a body to index them.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Rubric scores (repo-wide, 0–10) + evidence\n\n| Criterion | Score | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. Frontmatter completeness | **6** | 53–54/58 have version/author/license, but 4 unparseable, 5 name mismatches |\n| 2. Tag quality | **5** | All parseable skills ≥3 tags, but split across 2 schema locations (36 vs 22) |\n| 3. Relationship integrity | **2** | 24 dangling, 26 non-reciprocal, 6 missing — most of the graph is unreliable |\n| 4. Body structure | **3** | Overview 9/58, Verification 29/58, Pitfalls 36/58; 8 pure stubs |\n| 5. Portability/governance | **2** | 41/58 hardcoded paths; 3/58 declare env vars; no enforcement tooling |\n| 6. Freshness/signal | **8** | All 58 touched within the last 17 days; no abandonment |\n| 7. Uniqueness | **4** | 5 duplicate pairs (~10 skills, 17%), 2 contradictory |\n\n**Verification of the plan's measurability:** every number above came from a deterministic parser over the repo, so re-running the same audit after executing P1–P2 gives a before/after delta. Expected post-P1/P2 state: broken YAML 4→0, dangling refs 24→0, duplicates 5→0, schema split → unified, stubs 8→0-or-deprecated — which would move criteria 3, 4, 5, 7 from 2–4 into the 7–9 range. The CI linter then holds the line, which is the \"reduce future manual maintenance\" requirement. I've saved the baseline numbers and rubric to persistent memory (`kovaforge-skills-repo-review`) so a future session can re-measure against today.\n\n**Final self-score on this plan: 8/10.** It's grounded in full-coverage verified evidence (not sampling), every recommendation has a concrete mechanism and a measurable success criterion, and the prioritization correctly puts enforcement before cleanup. What keeps it from higher: three of the duplicate merges need owner decisions I can't make (which delegation map is correct; is `bw` deprecated; doccontrol ownership), the body-section counts are heading-regex-based and may slightly undercount, and I didn't validate that the skills' *scripts* actually run — script-level health is a follow-up audit.\n\nIf you want, I can execute P1 items 1–3 directly (linter, YAML fixes, dangling-ref repair) — they're mechanical and need no owner decisions.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e2486379-3fe7-4055-af04-c43d6f436df9","total_cost_usd":2.1212160000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":2102,"cache_creation_input_tokens":42305,"cache_read_input_tokens":388248,"output_tokens":17296,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":42305,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5270,"cache_read_input_tokens":50172,"cache_creation_input_tokens":284,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":284},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":958,"outputTokens"