hem **contradictory**: the bitwarden pair disagrees on whether the `bw` CLI is deprecated, and `delegation-research`/`research-delegation` have byte-identical descriptions but different routing tables (Milena/Nadia with pinned models vs a task-type split across Mikhail/Declan/Viktor) — which one an agent loads is a coin flip. |\n\n## 2. Prioritized plan (effort × impact)\n\n1. **Add a `validate-skills` linter + CI** (M effort, very high impact) — error tier: YAML parses, name==folder, required fields, ≥3 tags, related_skills resolve; warning tier: body sections, reciprocity, hardcoded paths. Pre-commit hook + GitHub Action. This is the only item that makes the others permanent.\n2. **Fix the 4 broken YAML frontmatters + 5 name mismatches** (XS, high) — one-line quoting fixes restore discovery for 4 skills.\n3. **Merge the 5 duplicate pairs, contradictory ones first** (S–M, high) — keep the richer skill, leave a tombstone SKILL.md with `superseded_by:` so crons and links don't break.\n4. **Script-fix the 39 dangling refs** (S, medium-high) — stripping the `vladislava-` prefix is mechanical; ~10 others (`codex`, `financial-report`, …) need hand resolution.\n5. **Pick one tag schema and migrate** (S, high) — recommend flipping AGENTS.md to top-level `tags:` (the 34-skill majority, simpler shape) and script-migrating the 20 hermes-schema skills.\n6. **Backfill the 10 stubs** (M, medium) — start with `playwright-cli` and `brainrepo`, each sitting on 9 orphaned reference/script files their bodies never index.\n7. **Path-portability sweep** (L, medium) — per the AGENTS.md Part 5 patch table; do the most-used skills first and let the linter's warning tier ratchet the rest rather than big-bang rewriting 45 skills.\n\n## 3. Governance to prevent recurrence\n\nCI-as-spec (rules not in the linter get ignored); a `TEMPLATE/SKILL.md` + scaffold script (stubs happen because authoring starts from blank); a rename policy requiring repo-wide `related_skills` grep (the entire dangling